<http://data.silknow.org/object/38958674-3e56-38c3-8b3a-2ceec9f86e25>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "\"I mestieri de lli mode a Venezia\", Venezia, 1997. pàg.100, núm.99: imatge a color. \"Voided velvet. Venice? 14th-15th centuries. On a crimson ground, Venetian coins (zechini) are made with weft theads of gold wrapped around yellow silk core; identical fabrics are in Florence and the Orient. The dress of Salome, depicted in a fourteenth-century mosaic in Saint Mark's basilica, is made with a textile of this type. VEnice, Mesei, Centro Studi di Storia del Tessuto e del Costume, fomerly Collection Guggenheim, nr.439\"."@es ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/0053c0fa-6ebb-3204-ae6f-c6e7af79d226> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "\"I mestieri de lli mode a Venezia\", Venezia, 1997. pàg.100, núm.99: imatge a color. \"Voided velvet. Venice? 14th-15th centuries. On a crimson ground, Venetian coins (zechini) are made with weft theads of gold wrapped around yellow silk core; identical fabrics are in Florence and the Orient. The dress of Salome, depicted in a fourteenth-century mosaic in Saint Mark's basilica, is made with a textile of this type. VEnice, Mesei, Centro Studi di Storia del Tessuto e del Costume, fomerly Collection Guggenheim, nr.439\"."@es .

